<!-- Challenges and Customization -->
<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 me-3 p-3" alt="Fee Management" /></div>
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/woman-tech-desk-chart-bureau.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Fee Management" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-8 Imgborder" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Fee Management Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>
                <p>Educational institutions can face disconnected systems, manual processes, inconsistent user journeys, limited visibility and operational complexity.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Disconnected Education Systems:</b> Connect student, learning, academic, examination, fee and administrative systems through integrated workflows.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Manual Administrative Work:</b> Automate repetitive data entry, approvals, notifications, scheduling and routine administrative activities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Limited Institutional Visibility:</b> Use centralized dashboards and reports to provide timely information to administrators and academic teams.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Complex Student Journeys:</b> Create consistent digital experiences across admissions, learning, examinations, student services and other education processes.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Data Management Concerns:</b> Use structured access controls, secure integrations and appropriate data-management practices.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>The Importance of Customization in Fee Management</b></h3>
                <p>Every educational institution has different academic structures, policies, departments, users and processes. Customization helps the solution fit the institution's operating model.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Customize Institutional Workflows:</b> Configure fee management processes around the institution's actual policies, departments and operating model.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Create Role-Based Experiences:</b> Provide relevant information and actions to administrators, educators, students, finance teams and other users.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Automate Notifications:</b> Configure alerts, reminders, approvals and workflow notifications for important academic and administrative events.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Build Custom Dashboards:</b> Provide role-specific reporting and visibility into key education and operational indicators.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Use User Feedback:</b> Continuously improve the solution based on real-world usage, feedback and institutional outcomes.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

